# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit the filled copy.
#
# There are two environment files, and they have different jobs:
#
#   .env.local   Gitignored. Local endpoints — the local PostgreSQL URL, the
#                blob backend, the data directory. Tooling writes to it
#                unprompted (`vercel link` appends a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN), which
#                is why it is not committed. This file documents everything it
#                would have held.
#
#   .env         THIS FILE, gitignored. Credentials, plus any personal
#                override of a .env.local value.
#
# Precedence: real environment variables > .env > .env.local. So exporting a
# variable in your shell beats both files, and .env beats the local
# defaults. `make env` prints what actually resolved.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ingestion
# Jamendo API client id (free, from https://devportal.jamendo.com/).
# Required only for `mode: jamendo` in config/tracks.json. The browser suite
# and `mode: offline` synthesize audio and need no credentials at all.
#
# This is the name Jamendo's own dashboard uses, so a block pasted from there
# works unedited. JAMENDO_CLIENT_ID is still accepted as an alias.
JAMENDO_API_CLIENT=
JAMENDO_API_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- overrides
# Everything below is already set in .env.local for local development. Set a
# value here only to point at something else — a deployed database, a real
# blob store, a scratch data directory.

# Supabase in production.
#
# You normally set NOTHING here. Vercel's Supabase integration provisions
# MIX_DB_POSTGRES_URL (and the Prisma / non-pooling variants) on the project,
# and the backend reads those directly — copying one into a second variable
# just creates two values that can disagree. Preference order is the pooled
# URL first, because a serverless function MUST use the transaction pooler
# (port 6543), not the direct connection: it opens many short-lived
# connections and would exhaust the direct limit. See docs/database.md.
#   MIX_DB_POSTGRES_URL              pooled, preferred
#   MIX_DB_POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL       same host, pgbouncer flag
#   MIX_DB_POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING  direct; last resort
#
# DJMIXER_DATABASE_URL overrides all of them. Setting it EMPTY is meaningful:
# it forces the local SQLite catalog, which is how run_tests.sh and CI keep
# the suite off a real database.
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<pw>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# DJMIXER_DATABASE_URL=

# `local` (filesystem, the default) or `vercel` (Vercel Blob).
# BLOB_BACKEND=

# Vercel Blob store id, as provisioned by the Blob integration. The public
# origin is derived from it — a store's host is its id minus the `store_`
# prefix, lowercased — so setting this alone is enough to serve audio, and the
# base URL cannot end up pointing at a different store than the token writes
# to.
BLOB_STORE_ID=

# Public origin of the blob store, e.g.
#   https://<store-id>.public.blob.vercel-storage.com
# Only needed to override the value derived from BLOB_STORE_ID — for a custom
# domain, or when moving to Cloudflare R2, which means changing only this.
# BLOB_BASE_URL=

# Vercel Blob read-write token, for uploads from the batch publisher. Not
# needed when the project is linked (the CLI uses OIDC then).
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# `public` (default) or `private`. A Blob store is created at one access level
# and REJECTS writes at the other, so this must match how the store was made.
#
# The app requires `public`: the audio endpoint 302s the browser straight to
# the object, which only works if the object is anonymously readable. A private
# store also proxies delivery through a Function instead of the CDN, which is
# roughly double-billed and puts audio back on the path the redirect exists to
# keep it off. `private` is accepted for uploads only — url_for() refuses to
# hand out a private URL rather than emit one that 404s in the browser.
# BLOB_ACCESS=public

# Where local blobs and the SQLite fallback live.
# DJMIXER_DATA=

# Which catalog to ingest.
# DJMIXER_TRACKS=
